{"name":"Porch Swing Beige","hex":"#d2cabe","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"porch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covered entrance to a building, whether taken from the interior, and forming a sort of vestibule within the main wall, or projecting without and with a separate roof. A porch often has chair(s), table(s) and swings.","A portico; a covered walk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porch"},{"term":"swing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rotate about an off-centre fixed point.","To dance."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act, or an instance, of swinging.","The manner in which something is swung."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swing"},{"term":"beige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour, variously defined from a pale brown, to a yellow greyish off-white.","Debeige; a kind of woollen or mixed dress goods."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a slightly yellowish gray colour, as that of unbleached wool.","Comfortably dull and unadventurous, in a way that suggests middle-class suburbia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beige"}],"entries":[{"title":"Swing (seat)","blocks":[{"text":"A swing is a seat or platform, suspended from chains, ropes, or bars, on which one or more people can swing back and forth for enjoyment or relaxation. Swings are a common piece of equipment at children's playgrounds and may also be found in yards or gardens, on porches, inside homes, or as freestanding public play equipment like the Estonian village swing. Swings have a long history in many different parts of the world and come in various types."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/MoSchaukel.jpg/330px-MoSchaukel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swing_(seat)","wikidata":"Q188688"},{"title":"Porch","blocks":[{"text":"A porch is a room or gallery located in front of an entrance to a building. A porch is placed in front of the façade of a building it commands, and forms a low front. Alternatively, it may be a vestibule or a projecting building that houses the entrance door of a building."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG/330px-Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porch","wikidata":"Q816741"},{"title":"Beige","blocks":[{"text":"Beige is variously described as a pale sandy fawn color, a grayish tan, a light-grayish yellowish brown, or a pale to grayish yellow. It takes its name from French, where the word originally meant natural wool that has been neither bleached nor dyed, hence also the color of natural wool."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg/330px-Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beige","wikidata":"Q843607"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Tire_swing%2C_near_Litchfield%2C_Connecticut_LCCN2012630791.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Tire_swing%2C_near_Litchfield%2C_Connecticut_LCCN2012630791.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Tire_swing%2C_near_Litchfield%2C_Connecticut_LCCN2012630791.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Tire_swing%2C_near_Litchfield%2C_Connecticut_LCCN2012630791.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Tire_swing%2C_near_Litchfield%2C_Connecticut_LCCN2012630791.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Tire_swing%2C_near_Litchfield%2C_Connecticut_LCCN2012630791.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia